    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "458102b0-e589-3f9b-91f8-d94a1b948870",
                "word": "intentionality",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ba951fce-be2f-4053-ad9b-e15aabb31151",
                        "entry_id": "458102b0-e589-3f9b-91f8-d94a1b948870",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "intentionalities"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1907d87c-6973-36b9-8328-ec0452d44880",
                        "entry_id": "458102b0-e589-3f9b-91f8-d94a1b948870",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The quality of being intentional."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8f3d0673-30a6-348d-bdd0-a5f5f46ba6c1",
                        "entry_id": "458102b0-e589-3f9b-91f8-d94a1b948870",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The characteristic of a mental state whereby it is about something, which relates to mental states in an analogous way as meaning relates to a word."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8eb874a-2208-43eb-bd39-c097345c1579",
                                "sense_id": "8f3d0673-30a6-348d-bdd0-a5f5f46ba6c1",
                                "text": "The naturalization of intentionality is an ongoing project in philosophy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "afca17cc-e4e2-471f-b362-1e88ddecd03d",
                                "sense_id": "8f3d0673-30a6-348d-bdd0-a5f5f46ba6c1",
                                "text": "As a preliminary formulation we might say: Intentionality is that property of many mental states and events by which they are directed at or about or of objects and states of affairs in the world."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd955740-3183-47cd-821e-355ca0133598",
                                "sense_id": "8f3d0673-30a6-348d-bdd0-a5f5f46ba6c1",
                                "text": "For phenomenology, the central feature of experience is a structure called \"intentionality,\" which correlates all things experienced with the mode of experience to which the experience is referenced."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8373c7d4-a4a9-46d1-a287-afd7858e353a",
                                "sense_id": "8f3d0673-30a6-348d-bdd0-a5f5f46ba6c1",
                                "text": "Causality in the Intentionality Model is in the agency of the child. It is the child who perceives, who apprehends, who constructs the intentional state, who acts to express it, and who interprets what others do (including what they say) to construct a new intentional state."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dcb07d98-a6d5-4d1b-aed3-fb31066adbcb",
                        "source_entry_id": "458102b0-e589-3f9b-91f8-d94a1b948870",
                        "source_sense_description": "(phil.) characteristic ...; ability to refer to sth.",
                        "target_lang_word": "intentionnalité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "intentionnalité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b0d0ce6-a7f5-3720-bb66-beb7fdb841ce",
                                        "entry_id": "23aded0a-4c22-37b3-b831-fb5fbe3c1d00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Caractère intentionnel d’une attitude, d’une pensée."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "548bfb42-2667-461c-82ef-194d929c77af",
                                                "sense_id": "2b0d0ce6-a7f5-3720-bb66-beb7fdb841ce",
                                                "text": "La théologie dissoudrait le dogme panthéiste en montrant ou croyant montrer que l’impersonnalité est contradictoire avec l’intentionnalité apparente des œuvres divines."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f52e6112-4379-4703-9131-b8539fea1fe0",
                                                "sense_id": "2b0d0ce6-a7f5-3720-bb66-beb7fdb841ce",
                                                "text": "Mais le parquet et le juge de la jeunesse doivent prendre en considération divers facteurs. Tels que la prise de conscience de la gravité de son acte pour le suspect, ses éventuels délits antérieurs et autres antécédents, et bien sûr l’intentionnalité."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21fb9298-dbc7-3833-bc4c-1d3066db58b0",
                                        "entry_id": "23aded0a-4c22-37b3-b831-fb5fbe3c1d00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relation psychologique active de la conscience à un objet existant, adaptée à un projet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c34f7d9-3c3b-4c12-aacb-e6361268d010",
                                                "sense_id": "21fb9298-dbc7-3833-bc4c-1d3066db58b0",
                                                "text": "La connaissance ou pure « représentation » n’est qu’une des formes possibles de ma conscience « de » cet arbre ; je puis aussi l’aimer, le craindre, le haïr, et ce dépassement de la conscience par elle-même, qu’on nomme « intentionnalité », se retrouve dans la crainte, la haine et l’amour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17b1546f-35f1-487d-a4ce-79068e8af160",
                                                "sense_id": "21fb9298-dbc7-3833-bc4c-1d3066db58b0",
                                                "text": "L’imposture et l’auto-illusion forment donc deux fabrications distinctes dont le point commun réside dans leur intentionnalité. À l'inverse, l’illusion constitue une « défaillance ordinaire » plus ou moins forte du cadre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
